# Testing and quality

Installed: ESLint (`npm run lint`), Prettier (`npm run format`), Vitest for unit/integration tests (`npm run test`, files `*.test.ts`), Playwright for browser tests (`npm run test:e2e`, files in `e2e/`). Run `npm run check` before saying work is done, plus `test:e2e` for UI changes. Theme contrast pairs are checked in `styles/theme-contrast.test.ts` on every `npm run test`; theme switching is covered in `e2e/theme.spec.ts`.

- **Unit** — domain rules and permission helpers.
- **Integration** — data access and transactions against a test database, never a shared or production one.
- **E2E** — critical paths (sign in, create property, record viewing) in a real browser.
- **Agency isolation** — every new query or mutation has a test proving another organisation is denied.
- If a test was skipped or tooling is missing, say the feature is **unverified**.

CI (when added) runs typecheck, lint, unit/integration tests, then e2e, plus a scheduled dependency audit.

Prettier owns formatting; do not hand-format. `components/ui` (shadcn output) and `AGENTS.md` are excluded from Prettier on purpose.
